 "notes": [
  "Kit2 read (lane kit-batch-8504-20261121) of the installed nieuwpoortstraat-126319, which stays untouched. Each south-front 3DBAG panel is its own group (alignWith 0) because face panels apply to a group's main panel only: walls[0] panel 115 (w03-179/w04-179 2025-09-26), walls[2] panel 268 and walls[3] panel 75 (w04-179, w05-179L 2021-03-24), walls[4] panel 38 with the two glazed sectional garage doors (w02-179 2025-09-26), walls[5] panel 103 (w02-179), walls[6] the canted south-east corner (w07-134 2025-09-26: one window per storey at the right of a storey-wide dark panel, brick pier left), walls[7] the Den Brielstraat end (w06-89 2021-02-24, no newer straight capture), walls[8] the 5.8 m west end surface 340 with the stair-hall door (w08-179L 2024-11-21).",
  "Every upper window sits in a dark grey panel stack (head panel over, spandrel panel under): accentPanels per bay, storeys 1-3, along 0.27-0.73, up 0.1-0.95, colour #42413f sampled from w04-179. Drawn with finish brick because the panel finish lands in the stone cell, which the city look lifts to L 0.62 and mixes 45 % into sandstone (the dark panels came out cream), and render floors at L 0.4 (the panels vanished into the measured wall); the brick finish keeps them darker than the wall but brown-grey, not the photo's charcoal (kit gap reported).",
  "Ground: a glazed plinth between piers per bay (plinth lights 2) in the wall brick with the brick band above it; the photo's piers are pale concrete, the band brick. No fascia, so the ACTION lettering of the installed recipe is dropped (a wall-mounted sign is at least 1.1 m tall in the kit; the real sign is about 0.35 m). Shop signs, DE MAKELAARS pin logo and posters not modelled.",
  "Palette: wall brick #756e67 hand-sampled from the overcast 2025-09-26 crops w03-179/w04-179 (the measure.ts run read trees and shadow as wall splits, #584924 and #1a1914, so it was reverted); listed in measured.groups so the look draws it as sampled. Attic #6e6b6a sampled from w04-179, drawn with wallFamily paint.",
  "No photo: the north courtyard side (Den Brielstraat, 120 m) and the west end wall (surface 58) have no panorama within range: otherWalls window-grid.",
  "Re-authored with the large-tier kit (lane kit-batch-8504-20261121, authored as nieuwpoortstraat-kit2-126319); blind against the previously installed recipe: the new recipe is closer."
 ]
}
